<title>UK: GECC sets 1.5 billion FFR 14-year bond. [CORRECTED 14:15 GMT]</title>
<headline>GECC sets 1.5 billion FFR 14-year bond. [CORRECTED 14:15 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Paribas.</p>
<p> BORROWER   GENERAL ELECTRIC CAPITAL CORP</p>
<p> AMT    1.5 BLN FFR   COUPON     5.75	MATURITY    25.AUG.11</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.009    PAY DATE    25.AUG.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  37.5 BP   REOFFER    99.009    SPREAD	+18 BP</p>
<p>(Lead manager corrects full fees from 40 bp to 37.5 bp.)  </p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    PARIS/LUX</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/FR</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND INTERPOLATED 6.50 PCT APRIL 2004 OAT AND</p>
<p>			    8.50 PCT DECEMBER 2012 OAT.</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF AN EMTN PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
